  "numerical_failure": {
    "category": "correctness",
    "affected_api": "pandas.core.nanops._wrap_results",
    "observed_behavior": "DataFrame.sum (axis=0 and axis=1) on overflowing timedelta64 silently returns an int64-max-saturated result with only a RuntimeWarning instead of raising OutOfBoundsTimedelta; Series([NaT, NaT]).sum(skipna=False) wrongly raises due to NaT sentinels accumulating past int64 bounds before masking.",
    "expected_behavior": "DataFrame.sum on overflowing timedelta64 should raise OutOfBoundsTimedelta, consistent with Series.sum; skipna=False reductions with NaT should still return NaT rather than a false overflow error.",
    "manifestation": "wrong_value",
    "trigger_conditions": [
      "DataFrame.sum over axis=0 or axis=1 on a timedelta64 column whose sum overflows int64 nanoseconds",
      "Series.sum with skipna=False on timedelta64 containing two or more NaT values (false raise, scalar branch)",
      "groupby.sum and resample.sum on overflowing timedelta64 still saturate silently and are not fixed by this change"
    ],
    "input_output_examples": [
      {
        "input": "x = pd.Series([pd.Timedelta(100000, \"days\"), pd.Timedelta(100000, \"days\")]); x.sum()",
        "buggy_output": "ValueError raised (inconsistent with DataFrame behaviour)",
        "expected_output": "OverflowError / OutOfBoundsTimedelta per the issue's request that all overflow errors be consistent",
        "value_kind": "exception",
        "source": "issue#43178"
      },
      {
        "input": "x*2 where x = pd.Series([pd.Timedelta(100000, \"days\"), pd.Timedelta(100000, \"days\")])",
        "buggy_output": "0   -13504 days +00:25:26.290448384\n1   -13504 days +00:25:26.290448384\ndtype: timedelta64[ns]",
        "expected_output": "an overflow error is raised",
        "value_kind": "exception",
        "source": "issue#43178"
      },
      {
        "input": "Series([NaT, NaT]).sum(skipna=False)",
        "buggy_output": "wrongly raises a false overflow error",
        "expected_output": "NaT",
        "value_kind": "exception",
        "source": "pr_body:PR#66227"
      }
    ],
    "oracle_clues": [
      "Expected behaviour is stated as raising OutOfBoundsTimedelta for DataFrame.sum overflow, matching Series.sum",
      "The issue requests all overflow related errors be of type OverflowError",
      "Silent RuntimeWarning is mentioned as the current DataFrame.sum symptom"
    ]
  },
  "numerical_characteristics": {
    "dtype": "timedelta64[ns] (m8[ns])",
    "precision": null,
    "magnitude": "Timedelta sums overflowing int64 bounds; example Series of two Timedelta(100000, 'days') values where x*2 yields -13504 days +00:25:26.290448384; NaT sentinels (iNaT) accumulating past int64 bounds when skipna=False",
    "tolerance": null,
    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "Passages show DataFrame.sum on overflowing timedelta64 silently saturated to int64 max with only a RuntimeWarning instead of raising OutOfBoundsTimedelta; Series.sum already raised.",
      "Issue example: x = pd.Series([pd.Timedelta(100000, 'days')]*2); x.sum() raised ValueError, pd.Timedelta(100000,'days')*2 raised OverflowError, x+x raised OverflowError, while x*2 silently wrapped to -13504 days +00:25:26.290448384.",
      "Fix adds guard overflow = np.abs(result) > lib.i8max in the ndarray branch of nanops._wrap_results, raising OutOfBoundsTimedelta('overflow in timedelta operation').",
      "Mask-aware check: positions in result_mask (destined to be NaT under skipna=False) are exempted from the raise and replaced by 0 before the m8[ns] cast.",
      "Regression case: df = DataFrame of three NaT m8[ns] values, df.sum(axis=..., skipna=False) must return dtype m8[ns] with all NaT; naive guard would falsely overflow because iNaT sentinels sum past int64 bounds.",
      "Scalar branch fix: Series([NaT, NaT]).sum(skipna=False) previously wrongly raised; the scalar check now includes result_mask."
    ],
    "reproduction_risks": [
      "Groupby.sum and resample.sum on overflowing timedelta64 still saturate silently per PR body, so they are outside this fix.",
      "The exact expected overflow value or the expected error message beyond 'overflow in timedelta operation' is not stated beyond the passages.",
      "Exception type expected for DataFrame.sum overflow is stated as OutOfBoundsTimedelta in the commit; the scalar-path error type varies (ValueError vs OverflowError) in the issue."
    ]
